  "body": "Found while working #1749 (the user's `sc_logo.camproj`). Related to #2180 (a band that only touches the shank top). This case is wider: the holder band starts below the stated shank top, beside the shank.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe tool T31 has `shank_d` 6.35 (the same as the cutter). Its drawn holder body starts 38.1 mm above the tip. The stated shank top is 65.278 mm. So the holder band stands beside the shank from 38.1 to 65.278 mm.\n\n`tool_body::judged` calls `HolderProfile::enclose` (`crates/tools/src/holder_profile.rs`). `enclose` widens the whole judged shank, from the flute top (14.478 mm) upward, to the band diameter (35 mm).\n\nResults on the user's project (forced regeneration, main `ce59ef446`):\n- The #1844 reach preflight refuses \"S1 Notch adaptive + terrace finish\". The refusal is false.\n- `verify` reports false `shank_hit` findings on four ops: 8138, 6884, 479 and 219 findings. They hold the post.\n\n## Expected\n\nThe judged body follows the drawn tool: the shank stays Ø6.35 below the holder foot. The holder band counts only where it is (from 38.1 mm up). A real holder collision must still be found and must still hold the post.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nThe refusal is safe, but it is wrong. The user cannot post a legal program. This blocks `sc_logo.camproj` from a clean post, whatever happens with #1749.\n\n## Safety\n\nDo not make the judged body smaller than the real tool anywhere. Pin both directions:\n- the false refusal goes away for a holder above the reach;\n- a holder band that does reach the stock still gives `shank_hit` / holder findings and holds the post.\n\nDone means: on a fixture like T31 (shank Ø6.35, holder from 38.1 mm, shank top 65.278 mm), the reach preflight and verify judge the shank at Ø6.35 below 38.1 mm; a test with a holder that touches the stock still refuses; #2180's case is checked too.\n",
